      "writtenOn": "2022-09-27T14:38:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e This seems a bit brittle as we don\u0027t enforce anywhere that a server\u0027s location/row contains \"-row-\", cf. in eqdfw and eqord now, even though we don\u0027t have any mgmt there.\n\nA bit brittle indeed, good catch re: eqdfw and eqord. I\u0027m not excited about the current \"parsing\" either, is there another field to get only the row \"name\" ? If we remove the split then we\u0027d get metrics with sth like the following, which IMHO isn\u0027t easy to use/read\n\n  {site\u003d\"eqiad\", rack\u003d\"a1\", row\u003d\"eqiad-row-a\"}\n\nHence the reason for split(), what do you think?",
      "parentUuid": "3d02f66a_982f87e6",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 96,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 96,
